    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/multi-media-specialist-ii-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Multi Media Specialist II - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Multi Media Specialist II 503823 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Sep 25 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Julie Hughes, 575-646-2874, juhughes@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The Social Media Specialist is responsible for planning, creating, and executing a comprehensive social media strategy for outreach for the New Mexico State University Cooperative Extension Service (CES) and Agricultural Experiment Station (AES). This position strengthens public awareness of Extension and research programs, amplifies research-based information, and supports outreach, engagement, and reputation-building efforts across diverse audiences including producers, families, communities, youth, students, policymakers, and partners. The Social Media Specialist works closely with educational media designers, Extension specialists, county offices, researchers, Ag Science Center faculty and staff, communicators, and leadership to translate complex information into engaging, accessible, and audience-centered social media content. Position Details Position Title: Multi Media Specialist II College/Division: Cooperative Extension Service Department: 310000-COOPERATIVE EXTENSION SERVICE Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate on education and experience Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: • Articulate social media strategies and part of communications and education outreach initiatives. This can include single, short running campaigns or larger unified social media campaigns for CES and AES that include multiple projects and impacts. • Plan editorial calendars that integrate research, programming, seasonal topics, campaigns, events, and impact stories. • Identify opportunities to communicate research discoveries, Extension expertise, community impact, and public value. • Create, schedule, and publish original social media content across multiple platforms (e.g., Facebook, Instagram, X, LinkedIn, YouTube, emerging platforms as appropriate). • Translate research findings and Extension programming into clear, engaging, and audience-appropriate social media posts. • Ensure content is accessible, inclusive, and compliant with university and federal accessibility standards. • Partner with Extension and research faculty on and off campus, county offices, and program staff to identify content ideas and elevate local and statewide efforts. • Provide guidance and best practices to Extension and AES staff contributing to social media or managing local accounts. • Coordinate social media efforts with central university communications and marketing teams as needed. • Work with team members to connect messaging across web and other outreach platforms. • Provide training and oversight of social media production. • Monitor social media channels and engage with audiences in a professional, timely, and mission-aligned manner. • Respond to comments and messages or route inquiries to appropriate subject-matter experts. • Support crisis communication or time-sensitive messaging when needed. • Track, analyze, and report on social media performance using platform analytics and other tools. • Use data and insights to refine strategy, improve engagement, and demonstrate impact. • Prepare regular performance summaries for leadership and stakeholders. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 4 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 2 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, journalism, public relations, agriculture, or a related field. • Demonstrated experience managing organizational social media accounts. • Strong writing and editing skills, with the ability to adapt tone and style for varied audiences. • Experience creating content for multiple social media platforms. • Ability to manage multiple projects, deadlines, and stakeholders simultaneously. • Familiarity with social media analytics, scheduling tools, and content management systems. • Experience with basic graphic design, photography, or video editing for social media. • Knowledge of branding, accessibility standards, and best practices for public institutions. • Experience working with Extension, research, higher education, agriculture, or public-sector organizations. • Strategic thinking and planning • Clear and engaging storytelling • Collaboration and relationship-building • Attention to detail and consistency • Commitment to public service and community engagement Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Similar Jobs Executive Assistant 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940600-DACC ACADEMIC SUPP DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Administrative Assistant Intermediate Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 500764-FS PROJECT DESIGN Join our team! Provide administrative support through communication, scheduling, requisitions, data management, reporting, and reconciliations. Coordinate meetings and events while serving as a liaison and supporting daily operations. Extension Specialist/ 4-H STEM Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 314000-4 H AND YOUTH DEVELOPMENT PGM UNIT The Cooperative Extension Service at NMSU is actively recruiting for a 4H STEM Specialist. This is a tenure-track, 12-month appointment.  Apply today! Student Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 380001-GRADUATE SCHOOL The Graduate School is seeking a detail-oriented and organized Student Program Coordinator, Sr. to support graduate students throughout their academic journey, from admission through graduation. This position processes and maintains student records and documentation related to admissions, academic milestones, program requirements, final examinations, thesis and dissertation submission, and degree certification. The successful candidate will work closely with students, faculty, and academic departments to interpret requirements, resolve record and processing issues, and ensure accurate and timely completion of Graduate School processes. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, sound judgment, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential for success in this role. Extension Specialist/Agronomist/ Soil Fertility 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 311200-EXTENSN PLANT SCIENCES Inviting applications for an Extension Agronomy/Soil Fertility Specialist, Assistant Professor (tenure-track, 12-month) position located at the Ag Science Center in Artesia, NM. CES County Program Assistant Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States 310600-ADMIN PRGM GUADALUPE CTY If you are interested in 4H, we have a job for you.  We are searching for a Program Assistant to work with the Cooperative Extension Agent to deliver programming and services to 4-H youth and other constituents.\n\n** This position is located in Guadalupe County, Santa Rosa, NM.** Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
