 H AND YOUTH DEVELOPMENT PGM UNIT The Cooperative Extension Service at NMSU is actively recruiting for a 4H STEM Specialist. This is a tenure-track, 12-month appointment.  Apply today! Student Program Coordinator Senior Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 380001-GRADUATE SCHOOL The Graduate School is seeking a detail-oriented and organized Student Program Coordinator, Sr. to support graduate students throughout their academic journey, from admission through graduation. This position processes and maintains student records and documentation related to admissions, academic milestones, program requirements, final examinations, thesis and dissertation submission, and degree certification. The successful candidate will work closely with students, faculty, and academic departments to interpret requirements, resolve record and processing issues, and ensure accurate and timely completion of Graduate School processes. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, sound judgment, and a commitment to excellent customer service are essential for success in this role. Extension Specialist/Agronomist/ Soil Fertility 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 311200-EXTENSN PLANT SCIENCES Inviting applications for an Extension Agronomy/Soil Fertility Specialist, Assistant Professor (tenure-track, 12-month) position located at the Ag Science Center in Artesia, NM. CES County Program Assistant Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States 310600-ADMIN PRGM GUADALUPE CTY If you are interested in 4H, we have a job for you.  We are searching for a Program Assistant to work with the Cooperative Extension Agent to deliver programming and services to 4-H youth and other constituents.\n\n** This position is located in Guadalupe County, Santa Rosa, NM.** Apply Now First Name (required) 26b7a5cc Last Name (required) 8538d104 Email (required) 4a916fe4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Diversity & Inclusion New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Quick Links About NMSU Contact Us Privacy Policy Search NMSU Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by New Mexico State University - Board of Regents . Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
