    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-social-work-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Position Details",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor Social Work - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Why NMSU? Aggie Perks Compensation and Benefits Applicant Resources View Jobs Applicant Login Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor Social Work 503999 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Closing at: Oct 25 2026 - 23:55 MDT Add to favorites View favorites Department Contact: Mary Nienow, 575-646-3043, mnienow@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: Assistant or Associate Professor — School of Social Work New Mexico State University. The NMSU School of Social Work, part of the College of Health, Education, and Social Transformation, invites applicants for Assistant or Associate Professor faculty position. We're seeking a scholar-educator who can teach across our undergraduate and graduate curriculum — in person, online synchronous, and online asynchronous — grounded in CSWE/EPAS competencies. The ideal candidate brings an active, fundable research agenda, a strong record of mentoring students, and a genuine commitment to equity-centered social work education. Rank and tenure status will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and record of scholarship, teaching, and service. NMSU is a Hispanic-Serving Institution with deep ties to Native American communities across the Southwest; candidates with experience in culturally responsive pedagogy, Indigenous social work practice, bilingual (Spanish/English) proficiency, and academic leadership are especially encouraged to apply. Required: PhD in Social Work; MSW from a CSWE-accredited program; teaching experience across delivery formats; a research agenda complementing existing faculty strengths; and a demonstrated commitment to DEI. To apply: Submit a letter of interest, CV, teaching philosophy, research statement, three references, and unofficial transcripts. Position Details Position Title: Assistant or Associate Professor College/Division: College of Hlth, Educ & Soc Trans Department: 370300-SOCIAL WORK Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: 75,000-90,000, Commensurate with rank & qualifications Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The faculty member must be able to provide undergraduate and graduate instruction across the School's curriculum, delivered in in-person, online synchronous, and online asynchronous formats, and grounded in CSWE/EPAS competencies. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of scholarship appropriate to rank, including peer-reviewed publication and, where applicable, external funding or grant-seeking activity. The faculty member will also mentor undergraduate/graduate students and contribute to advising. Additional responsibilities include service to the School, the University, the profession, and the broader community, along with a demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusive pedagogy. Rank and tenure status will be determined based on the candidate's qualifications, experience, and record of scholarship, teaching, and service. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Completed doctorate degree in social work area Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: • An established record of peer-reviewed scholarship and external research funding, with credentials appropriate to appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor • Experience teaching in a PhD-level social work curriculum • Active or license-eligible New Mexico social work licensure appropriate to the position's teaching focus • A minimum of three years of post-MSW social work practice experience • Experience with academic leadership, program coordination, or committee service • Experience mentoring students and junior faculty • Experience working with Hispanic-Serving Institutions or similarly diverse student populations Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1b94fc3b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 370300-SOCIAL WORK 370300-SOCIAL WORK Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) b8677ff2 Last Name (required) 84961f28 Email (required) 2b47eb53 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Executive Assistant 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940600-DACC ACADEMIC SUPP DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Administrative Assistant Intermediate Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 500764-FS PROJECT DESIGN Join our team! Provide administrative support through communication, scheduling, requisitions, data management, reporting, and reconciliations. Coordinate meetings and events while serving as a liaison and supporting daily operations. Extension Specialist/ 4-H STEM Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 314000-4 H AND YOUTH DEVELOPMENT P